1
00:00:00,033 --> 00:00:12,235
(Q31) Today, I want to talk about self-regulatory focus theory and how the actions of leaders can affect the way followers approach different situations.

2
00:00:12,235 --> 00:00:18,575
Self-regulatory focus theory is a theory developed by Tori Higgins.

3
00:00:18,575 --> 00:00:27,505
He says that a person's focus at any given time is to either approach pleasure or avoid pain.

4
00:00:27,505 --> 00:00:36,788
These are two basic motivations that each and every one of us has, and they cause us to have different kinds of goals.

5
00:00:36,788 --> 00:00:43,504
[Q31答案句] Promotion goals in different life situations emphasise achievement.

6
00:00:43,504 --> 00:00:50,295
(Q32) Prevention goals are oriented towards the avoidance of punishment.

7
00:00:50,295 --> 00:01:01,093
In a specific situation, our thoughts might focus more on promotion goals or more on prevention goals.

8
00:01:01,093 --> 00:01:08,638
The theory suggests that two factors affect which goals we are focusing on.&nbsp;

9
00:01:08,638 --> 00:01:30,655
[Q32答案句] First, there is a chronic factor. This factor is connected to a person's personality and says that each person has a basic tendency to either focus more on promotion goals or focus more on prevention goals as part of his or her personality.

10
00:01:30,655 --> 00:01:43,883
(Q33) [Q33答案句] Second, there is a situational factor which means that the context we are in can make us more likely to focus on one set of goals or the other.

11
00:01:43,883 --> 00:01:54,168
(Q34) [Q34答案句] For example, we are more likely to be thinking about pleasure and to have promotion goals when we are spending time with a friend.

12
00:01:54,168 --> 00:02:10,395
(Q35) In contrast, if we are working on an important project for our boss, we are more likely to try to avoid making mistakes and therefore have more prevention goals in our mind.

13
00:02:10,395 --> 00:02:19,214
Research has shown that the goals we are focusing on at a given time affect the way we think.

14
00:02:19,214 --> 00:02:29,683
[Q35答案句] For example, when focusing on promotion goals, people consider their ideal self, their aspirations and gains.

15
00:02:29,683 --> 00:02:36,004
(Q36) They don't think about what they can lose, so they think in a happier mode.

16
00:02:36,004 --> 00:02:39,795
They feel more inspired to change.

17
00:02:39,795 --> 00:02:46,508
When people are focusing on prevention goals, they think about their "ought" self.

18
00:02:46,508 --> 00:02:48,936
What are they supposed to be?

19
00:02:48,936 --> 00:02:51,666
What are people expecting from them?

20
00:02:51,666 --> 00:02:55,700
They consider their obligations to others.

21
00:02:55,700 --> 00:03:07,842
As a result, they experience more anxiety and try to avoid situations where they could lose.

22
00:03:07,842 --> 00:03:27,636
[Q36答案句] Now that I have talked about the two focuses and how they affect people, I want to look at the idea that the way leaders behave, or their style of leading, can affect the focus that followers adopt in a specific situation.

23
00:03:27,636 --> 00:03:37,619
(Q37) In talking about leadership, we often mention transformational leaders and transactional leaders.

24
00:03:37,619 --> 00:03:45,354
[Q37答案句] Transformational leaders, when interacting with their followers, focus on their development.

25
00:03:45,354 --> 00:03:51,511
(Q38) In their words and actions transformational leaders highlight change.

26
00:03:51,511 --> 00:03:57,415
[Q38答案句] Their speech is passionate and conveys a definitive vision.

27
00:03:57,415 --> 00:04:04,052
(Q39) All of these things can encourage followers to think about what could be.

28
00:04:04,052 --> 00:04:11,306
In other words, they inspire a promotion focus in their followers.

29
00:04:11,306 --> 00:04:23,950
[Q39答案句] In contrast, transactional leaders focus on developing clear structures that tell their followers exactly what is expected of them.

30
00:04:23,950 --> 00:04:40,687
(Q40) While they do explain the rewards people will get for following orders, they emphasise more how a follower will be punished or that a follower won't get rewarded if his or her behaviour doesn't change.

31
00:04:40,687 --> 00:04:46,617
In short, they emphasise the consequences of making a mistake.

32
00:04:46,617 --> 00:04:54,651
This emphasis will clearly lead followers to focus on avoiding punishment and problems.

33
00:04:54,651 --> 00:04:58,914
This is clearly a prevention focus.

34
00:04:58,914 --> 00:05:08,290
In conclusion, it is important to understand that one focus is not necessarily better than the other one.

35
00:05:08,290 --> 00:05:17,431
[Q40答案句] For a designer who works in a field where a lot of innovation is needed, a promotion focus is probably better.

36
00:05:17,431 --> 00:05:31,246
In contrast, a prevention focus which causes people to work more cautiously and produce higher quality work might be very appropriate for a job like a surgeon, for example.

37
00:05:31,246 --> 00:05:33,746
The main point of the research, though, is that the actions of leaders can greatly influence whether people approach a situation with more of a promotion focus or more of a prevention focus.

